// The botshare base's Gemini 336L, rendered by the simulation as an rgbd
// producer, color and depth aligned because both come from one rendered
// camera. The relay pairs into the simulation's rgbd_cameras slot and
// presents the rgbd_camera contract, and describes the camera through
// camera_profile. The slot holds any
// number of pairs: the simulation tells a pair's robot by its copy and its
// camera by the relay's name in that copy, the instance id written here.
//
// The relay also holds a control slot for the simulation's camera response
// model (sim_camera_control), which forwards the controls a consumer sets
// on the camera to the simulation's model of that camera. Waldo implements
// it, and refuses each control of this camera, whose entry names no device,
// so the relay binds it there; MuJoCo and Isaac Sim have no response model,
// so the slot is written vacant and every camera control refuses on them.
//
// The relay names in every picture the camera's frame, which the
// initializer's sensor_mounts gives for the relay's instance id.
//
// The launcher binds the rig to the stack's MCP endpoint, the rendered relay
// listed with its profile and geometry. The simulation renders the camera
// where its botshare_base model's description places it on the chassis,
// at that model's intrinsics and rate.
{
  peppy_schema: "launcher_fragment/v1",

  deployments: [
    {
      source: { name: "sim_rgbd_camera", tag: "v1" },
      instances: [
        { instance_id: "base_camera",
          links: {
            simulation: "simulation_inst/rgbd_cameras",
            control: { vacant: "this simulation has no camera response model; every camera control refuses" },
            sensor_mounts: "init_inst",
          },
          framework: { clock: "simulation" } },
      ],
    },
  ],

  adjustments: [
    // Waldo implements the camera response model: the relay binds it there.
    { target: "base_camera", when: { simulation: "waldo" }, set_links: { control: "simulation_inst" } },
  ],
}
